{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.1ac161f196805b2bf5703abb.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The assessment concerns one identified promotional offer by an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.1ac161f196805b2bf5703abb.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The result is a screen for the selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control only, evaluated when scope is true.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.1ac161f196805b2bf5703abb.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Gift, discount and product-link classifications must be supplied from evidence and judgment; unknown classifications remain unknown.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.1ac161f196805b2bf5703abb.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"No independent requirement to prove actual investor distraction is added: the text states distraction as the purpose and rationale.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"b1ad6bbab35243fcafd6df8ac7c230787789ab738ce026005aad57af5e6a0d68","candidate_id":"candidate.0eeb944a32594b8dbde075fc5c65867f","controlled_language":"For the selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control, an in-scope distributor should not offer a gift in a client promotion connected to a specific investment product or particular product type unless the benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges. The linked-product-type explanation carries the same exception. Structured-product classification and section 103 authorisation are separate issues. The strongest unresolved issue is classification of borderline rebates and incentives, which the retained text and absent FAQ do not settle.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["exceptions"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":[],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"The supported reading attaches the exception to qualifying fee discounts and reaches both individual-product and product-type promotions. For a concrete classification boundary, consider a cash payment after subscribing to funds from one fund house, equal to the subscription fee. If it genuinely reduces that fee, the selected screen passes; if it is a separate gift merely measured by the fee, it fails. The supplied text does not decide which classification applies, so these are unresolved applications rather than two asserted legal rules. By contrast, excluding all fund-house-wide promotions because no single fund is named is contradicted by the express example.","run_id":"run.d6106e5450c749a58852e36e6f81a6e0","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"7b78bffd5267abb04c58ab204d1e34f621dc3fb03008be1b35980abcaa535ba4","source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u14","u15","u30"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: fee-discount exception and product connection"}